{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderRungAmplification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderRungAmplification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c3Of_sub_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c3Of_sub_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderRungAmplification.lean#L94-L119","doc":"**A rung gap is nonzero exactly when the cosines differ** (given a\nnonvanishing overall scale). So an enormous `c₃` gap carries no information\nbeyond \"the cosines differ\" — the size of it is `u⁻³`, not evidence about the\nconventions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c3Of_sub_mul_u_cubed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c3Of_sub_mul_u_cubed","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderRungAmplification.lean#L81-L92","doc":"**The amplification factor is exactly `u⁻³`.**\n\nMultiplying the rung gap by `u³` leaves a quantity with no `u`-scaling in it\nat all beyond the `(1 − u²)` prefactor — so the `1/u³ = 1.6×10⁶` at the\nsubstrate anchor is the entire magnification, not a coincidence of scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c3Of_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c3Of_sub","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderRungAmplification.lean#L67-L79","doc":"**The amplification identity.**\n\nThe gap between the rungs extracted under two conventions is the gap between\ntheir cosine *reciprocals*, scaled by `Q_c/(Q_A(1−u²))` and divided by `u³`.\nNothing else contributes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c3Of_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c3Of_congr","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderRungAmplification.lean#L61-L65","doc":"**The convention enters only through the cosine.** Two conventions with\nthe same `cos(α_eff)` give the same rung, whatever else differs about them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.c3Of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.c3Of","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderRungAmplification.lean#L52-L59","doc":"The ladder's extracted third rung as a function of the N=1 cosine.\n\nMirrors `c3 = (Q_codata / Q_N2 − 1) / u³` with `Q_N2 = Q_A · cs · (1 − u²)`,\nwhich is the extraction in `qbeta_ck_cache.py`. `cs` stands for\n`cos(α_eff)`: it is the **only** place a Markov convention enters, since\n`Q_A`, `b` and `u` are built from the Hoefsmit couplings. ","signatureChunk":0}]}